  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\n[Respond to base URL changes](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/urls-and-fetching.html#respond-to-base-url-changes) creates _newResult_ and calls [update speculation rules](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#update-speculation-rules), but nothing sets the `script` element's result to _newResult_. So after one base URL change:\n\n- A second base URL change removes the original rule set again (a no-op) and appends another one, leaving the rule set from the first change in the document's speculation rule sets.\n- Removing the `script` element [unregisters](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#unregister-speculation-rules) the original result, so the current rule set stays registered.\n\nMaybe respond to base URL changes should set the element's result to _newResult_ after updating.\n",
